Subject: [PATCH 0/1] Input: rmi4 - retain resume after a failed sleep command

A failed RMI sleep command currently leaves the I2C supplies disabled while
returning an error from system suspend. The PM core does not mark this device
suspended and therefore skips its resume callback. Complete the callback after
powering down, matching the runtime-suspend behavior, so ordinary resume and
unwind after another device fails can restore the transport.

This is an unsigned review draft based on Input master/next at
8e16f8bbf1bd528975fd6f4081eaf00513c1d83e. It adapts the downstream fix
6d3c6c42f7bbfcc93dfac4e46da6debe23e4f3bd without requiring the downstream
reset-GPIO or panel-follower additions. The receiving tree's allocation and
power-management APIs are preserved; only system suspend changes.

Validation:
- 119 lifecycle cases using the extracted actual four I2C transport callbacks
  pass ASan and UBSan. The original code and four independent regression
  controls fail the expected behavioral assertions. The PM-core decision is
  source-checked and modeled; this fixture does not execute the kernel PM core.
- Unmodified base and draft ARM objects compile with Clang 21.1.8, W=1, KCFI
  and full zlib-compressed DWARF5 without diagnostics. All four callback type
  words match. The normalized configuration is byte-identical.
- Strict checkpatch passes with only sign-off checking disabled. The exported
  patch replays to the exact draft tree.

Earlier Fx0 s2idle testing exercised the same return-value fix together with
separate touch-panel and MDP5 changes. It does not qualify this standalone
maintainer tree. Full kernel/module links, this tree's physical boot and suspend,
other RMI hardware and regulator-disable failures remain unqualified. Resume
supply and RMI-function errors are preserved and exercised by the host fixture.

This draft was prepared with an AI coding assistant. Human review and DCO
certification are pending. No Signed-off-by or Tested-by tag is added by the
assistant. No email or upstream PR has been sent.

